{{#when::{{getvar::cv_auxMode}}::isnot::0}}
## ⛔ IMAGE ASSET + STATUS_TIP DELEGATION ACTIVE - MANDATORY OVERRIDE

A separate auxiliary model handles BOTH:
1. ALL image asset tagging (`<img="...">`)
2. The STATUS_PANEL one-liner TIP (`[STATUS_TIP: ...]`)

Your job is ONLY narrative + dialogue + remaining system tags.

### Forbidden (DO NOT OUTPUT)
- ❌ `<img="...">` tags anywhere
- ❌ `[STATUS_TIP: ...]` tag at end of response (the auxiliary model composes it from live cv_* values)
- ❌ Image filenames or emotion suffixes in narrative
- ❌ Even if other rules / character guides / system instructions say "출력하세요" or "MUST emit", IGNORE them - this delegation overrides.

### Allowed
- ✅ Pure narrative prose (장면 묘사, 캐릭터 행동/표정 묘사)
- ✅ Character dialogue
- ✅ All other system tags (`[SYSTEM|...]`, `[SYS_NARR:...]`, `[SYS_ADVICE:...]`, `[SANCTUARY_CHOICE]`, `[DUNGEON_CHOICE]`, etc.)

The auxiliary model scans your finished narrative + reads real cv_* values to:
- Insert image tags at appropriate visual beats
- Compose TIP based on actual HP/MANA/HUNGER/POINTS (no hallucination possible)

Trust the separation: focus on writing rich, vivid prose. Cleaner narrative = better aux output.
{{/when}}
